[00:29.60] The rusted chains of prison moons are shattered by the sun
[00:36.62] I walk a road, horizons change, the tournament's begun
[00:44.38] The purple piper plays his tune, the choir softly sing
[00:51.53] Three lullabies in an ancient tongue for the court of the crimson king
[01:06.20] 
[01:25.28] The keeper of the city keys ut shutters on the dreams
[01:32.35] I wait outside the pilgrim's door with insufficient schemes
[01:39.93] The black queen chants, the funeral march, the cracked brass bells will ring
[01:47.27] To summon back the fire witch to the court of the crimson king
[01:57.07] 
[03:20.57] The gardener plants an evergreen whilst trampling on a flower
[03:27.35] I chase the wind of a prism ship to taste the sweet and sour
[03:34.86] The pattern juggler lifts his hand, the orchestra begin
[03:41.86] As slowly turns the grinding wheel in the court of the crimson king
[03:58.18] 
[05:31.45] On soft gray mornings widows cry, the wise men share a joke
[05:38.56] I run to grasp divining signs to satisfy the hoax
[05:45.72] The yellow jester does not play, but gently pulls the strings
[05:53.09] And smiles as the puppets dance in the court of the crimson king
[06:03.02] 